# ls(1)

## NAME

ls - list directory contents

## SYNOPSIS

    ls [-1adlF] [file...]

## DESCRIPTION

Lists the entries of each directory (default `.`) in name order. On a terminal, names are arranged in columns to fit the screen width.

At most 2048 entries and 64 KiB of names are listed per directory.

## OPTIONS

- `-a`: include names starting with `.`
- `-d`: list directories themselves, not their contents
- `-l`: long format: type, size, modification time (UTC) and name
- `-1`: one name per line
- `-F`: append `/` to directory names

## EXIT STATUS

- `0`: success
- `1`: an error occurred for some operand
- `2`: usage error

## SEE ALSO

du(1), mkdir(1)
